# Build output. Covers everything Gradle generates in both projects: generated-src (the ANTLR
# parser), classes, test-results, reports, the jacoco *.exec files and the assembled jars.
build/
cli/build/
.gradle/

# Maven's output directory. Still ignored while pom.xml exists, so a `mvn` run during the
# Gradle transition cannot dump 656 untracked files into `git status`. Remove this line in the
# same commit that deletes pom.xml.
target/

# The wrapper script and JAR ARE committed, deliberately: `./gradlew` must work in a fresh
# checkout. That is what lets the Makefile be the only entry point and CI use the same Gradle
# version a developer does.

# IDE
.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/
.settings/
.classpath
.project

# Editor / OS noise
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The two Ewing-lab fixtures are the ONLY test data not committed (Correction C26).
#
# data/CONVERSION_NOTES.md records them as "unstated licence": they are downloaded from
# ewinglab.org, which publishes no redistribution terms, so we do not republish them.
# Everything else under src/test/resources/ IS committed, deliberately -- see C26 (CI could not
# see the fixtures at all, so every parity assertion silently skipped and CI proved nothing).
#
# Their GOLDENS are committed, and that is not an inconsistency: loader-parity dumps hold
# per-scan counts, hex sums and SHA-256 digests; query-result goldens hold matched-scan metadata.
# Neither contains a peak array, so no spectra are redistributed.
#
# `scripts/fetch-fixtures.sh` downloads both into this directory, and CI runs it and caches the
# result. Fixtures.require() FAILS with that instruction when they are missing -- it must never
# skip, which is the regression C26 exists to prevent.
src/test/resources/data/DP00570_F02.mzxml
src/test/resources/data/DP00570_F02.mgf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DO NOT ignore src/test/resources/reference_parses/*.json
#
# Those 46 files look like temp output because of their hash-suffixed names
# (QUERY_scaninfo_MS1DATA__WHERE_MS1MZ_425.2898TOLERA___106d511f8de4ae41364fbece4838e2c8.json)
# but that is MassQL's own test-corpus naming and they are REQUIRED fixtures.
# ParseConformanceTest reads every one and asserts the count is exactly 46, so ignoring them
# turns the parser conformance suite into a vacuous pass and then a hard failure.
#
# Same for reference_parses/corpus-manifest.tsv and dependency-audit.txt: both are
# checked-in review artifacts, not generated noise. The audit file is content-deterministic
# (no timestamp) precisely so it only shows a diff when the closure actually changes.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
